  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output A.1. Enhanced decent work statistics using innovative sources and statistical standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Botswana, through the Human Resource Development Council (HRDC), has worked towards the implementation of the Labour Market Information System (LMIS). This work is completed. Durring the biennium, the ILO provided technical capcuty throughout the whole processs.The following activities have been conducted :

ILO support was provided for: A Data Production workshop was held in May 2022  to review labour market indicators (source, formula, definition, classification, disaggregation) for all data producers and users in the country.
The LMIS.Stat application software has been installed in the LMIS Unit of the Human Resource Development Council (HRDC).
Trainings have been conducted for LMI officials focusing on IT, data and metadata.
Configuration of structural metadata and initial loading of data undertaken.
Workshop on SDMX and Data Modelling have been conducted by ILO.
Special workshop conducted in Turin by LMIS team, to support countries that are about to launch LMIS. The staff from HRDC attended the workshop. 
ILO has taken and completed all steps necessary for LMIS implementation. Launch of the LMIS  was held in September 2023</narrative>
   </description>
